					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dolphinslugchugger" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1969477); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1969477&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606380126" alt="DolphinSlugchugger" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1969477)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dolphinslugchugger" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1969477); return false;" >DolphinSlugchugger</a></span> <span class="odate time_1547297974 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">12 Jan 2019 12:59</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4116848">
									

<p>Deliberate. The year isn't a reference to the scp 2055, just intended as another layer of the in-joke.</p>
<p>As for P-9055, it's a holdover from the first go at the article, where the P is intended to indicate a provisional containment vessel instead of a permanent one. I ended up keeping it because, provisional or not, it still very much is significant in-universe that it's placed where it was. It's not in the containment procedures, however, because the narrator at first found the specific locker inconsequential, and it became completely irrelevant once the narrator realized it was a joke.</p>

